Template: cmnd-linux/server-ip
Type: string
Default: auto
Description: IPv4 address CMND should use:
 Enter an IPv4 address already assigned to this server. Use "auto" to select the first active non-loopback IPv4 address.

Template: cmnd-linux/database-mode
Type: select
Choices: auto, existing, isolated
Default: auto
Description: Database integration mode:
 "auto" reuses an existing MySQL service only if it passes the CMND compatibility gate; otherwise it uses the isolated pinned MySQL runtime. "existing" refuses fallback. "isolated" never changes an existing database service.

Template: cmnd-linux/database-admin-user
Type: string
Default: root
Description: Existing database administrator user:
 Used only when an existing database requires password authentication. The password is never stored in CMND persistent configuration.

Template: cmnd-linux/database-admin-password
Type: password
Description: Existing database administrator password:
 Leave blank to let auto mode use the isolated database fallback. This value is used only during package configuration and is cleared after the activation attempt.

Template: cmnd-linux/apache-mode
Type: select
Choices: auto, host, standalone
Default: auto
Description: Apache integration mode:
 "auto" attaches a CMND-owned fragment to an already-running Debian/Ubuntu Apache service, otherwise it runs an isolated CMND Apache process. Existing unrelated sites and listeners are preserved.

Template: cmnd-linux/accept-legacy-runtime
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Accept CMND's legacy PHP 5.6 / MySQL 5.7 compatibility runtime?
 The original Philips CMND 7.5.9 application requires legacy compatibility components. They are isolated where practical and should not be exposed directly to the Internet.
